@startuml
title Figure 2. ResourceHive Container and Service Architecture
top to bottom direction

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowFontSize 14
skinparam TitleFontSize 18
skinparam shadowing false

actor User

rectangle "Frontend Hosting" {
  component "Marketing Website\nNext.js" as Marketing
  component "Web Application\nNext.js" as WebApp
}

node "Backend Host" {
  component "API Gateway\nNginx" as Gateway
  component "Identity Service\nNestJS" as Identity
  component "Resource Service\nNestJS" as Resource
  component "Booking Service\nNestJS" as Booking
  component "Notification Service\nNestJS" as Notification
}

database "Shared PostgreSQL" as Database
cloud "Email Provider" as Email

User --> Marketing : HTTPS
User --> WebApp : HTTPS
Marketing --> WebApp : Open application
WebApp --> Gateway : API requests\nHttpOnly JWT cookie

Gateway -down-> Identity : /auth/*
Gateway -down-> Resource : /organizations/*\n/memberships/*\n/resources/*
Gateway -down-> Booking : /slots*\n/bookings*\n/points*\n/resources/{id}/slots
Gateway -down-> Notification : /notifications*\nSocket.IO upgrade

Identity -[hidden]right- Resource
Identity -[hidden]down- Booking
Resource -[hidden]down- Notification
Booking -[hidden]right- Notification

Identity --> Database
Resource --> Database
Booking --> Database
Notification --> Database
Identity --> Email : Verification email

note bottom of Gateway
The gateway only routes requests. Protected services verify
the JWT locally and perform their own authorization checks.
end note
@enduml
